 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Function",
   "page": 9,
   "text": "Y follows A: a high input gives a high output, a low input a low output."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Input thresholds and up translation",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The input switching points sit lower than standard CMOS levels for the supply, so a 1.8 V logic signal is read as high with VCC = 3.3 V (VIH 1.37 V min at VCC = 3 V to 3.3 V). The output then swings to VCC, giving 1.8 V to 3.3 V, 1.5 V to 2.5 V, 1.2 V to 1.8 V or 3.3 V to 5.0 V translation with VCC set to the output level."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Down translation",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The input accepts up to 5.5 V with any VCC in range, so a higher-voltage signal is brought down to the VCC level: 3.3 V to 1.8 V, 3.3 V to 2.5 V, or 5 V to 3.3 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The output level follows VCC and is CMOS compatible with the AUP1G and LVC1G families. Drive is limited to 8 mA at 5.0 V, 7 mA at 3.3 V and 3 mA at 1.8 V; the modest drive reduces reflections, overshoot and undershoot on the line. Its timing is specified to 50 MHz with VCC = 3.3 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Supply current with a mid-level input",
   "page": 5,
   "text": "ΔICC, the added supply current with one input at a level away from the rails: up to 1.35 mA at 25 °C (1.5 mA over temperature) with the input at 0.3 V or 3.4 V and VCC = 5.5 V, and up to 10 µA with it at 0.3 V or 1.1 V and VCC = 1.8 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Unused inputs",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "Every unused input is held at VCC or GND."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Robustness",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Latch-up immunity above 250 mA per JESD 17. ESD tested to JESD 22: HBM 2000 V (A114-B, class II), MM 200 V (A115-A), CDM 1000 V (C101)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Pinout",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The part uses a standard logic pinout."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Packages and mounting",
   "page": 16,
   "text": "Both packages are rated MSL level 1 at 260 °C peak reflow. DBV follows JEDEC MO-178; DCK falls within JEDEC MO-203 variation AA. DCK body dimensions leave out mold flash and protrusion, which add at most 0.15 mm per side."
  }
 ],
